{{Quote|Bad news, Tenno. The Stalker has found others as twisted as himself. He calls them his Acolytes and he's sent them after me! Shh! I have to be very quiet, they cloak! They could be hiding anywhere! Even listening to this!|[[Alad V]] during [[Operation: Shadow Debt]]}}
{{Tocright}}
<section begin="intro"/>
The '''Acolytes''' are mysterious, twisted, sinister [[Warframe]]s<ref>''"Twisted Warframes that follow the Stalker in pursuit of vengeance, the Acolytes will not stop until they are destroyed or until the Stalker’s mission is fulfilled. Gather your Squad and hunt them down one by one before the hunter becomes the hunted."''<br>[https://www.warframe.com/en/news/the-acolytes-return The Acolytes Return]</ref> that are devoted to the [[Stalker]], taking the appearance and abilities of different Warframes while bearing the distinctive helmet of their master. They were first introduced in the [[Operation: Shadow Debt]] event, and would make sporadic reappearances afterwards.

As of {{ver|29.5}}, Acolytes became a permanent addition to the game, making appearances in [[The Steel Path]] missions and dropping {{Resource|Steel Essence}}.
<section end="intro"/>

==Lore==
Other than serving the [[Stalker]], little is known about the Acolytes.

===[[Operation: Shadow Debt]]===
For [[Alad V]]'s interference in [[The Second Dream]], the Acolytes are sent to dispatch him. Alad V invokes his favor from The Second Dream to have the [[Tenno]] safeguard him from the Acolytes.

==Mechanics==
Acolytes can only receive up to 4 stacks of any [[Status Effect]] with the exception of {{D|Impact}} which can stack up to 3 times, and {{D|Radiation}} only amplifies the damage the Acolyte receives from allied units and does not enable friendly fire unless those allies themselves are inflicted by the status.

===[[The Steel Path]]===
Acolytes typically spawn in non-[[Archwing]], non-[[Assassination]], non-[[Ascension]], non-[[Dark Refractory]], non-[[Duviri]] and non-[[Empyrean|Railjack]] Steel Path missions once every 3-8 minutes on average. They are guaranteed to drop 2 [[Steel Essence]], as well as one random [[Arcane_Enhancement#The_Steel_Path_Arcanes|Steel Path Arcane]] ({{Arcane|Primary Deadhead}}, {{Arcane|Primary Dexterity}}, {{Arcane|Primary Merciless}}, {{Arcane|Secondary Deadhead}}, {{Arcane|Secondary Dexterity}}, or {{Arcane|Secondary Merciless}}), upon defeat.

